  "description": "Authoritative fidelity/provenance registry for every artwork reachable from an active sign question. Schedule pages refer to the 2023 consolidated Province of Nova Scotia Schedule of Official Traffic Signs. Official crops use image crops from public/signs/ns-official as the learner-facing artwork (status official-crop); provenance distinguishes ns-schedule, ns-driver-handbook, and ns-work-zone-manual sources. Remaining signs keep original SVG assembled in src/signs/registry.tsx pending a crop (status legacy-pending-crop). RB-1 is a variable-number sign: the Schedule fixes the design and lets the numeral change per location, so both speed variants keep designation RB-1 and are told apart by variant. The optional `asset` field names the OFFICIAL_CROPS key holding that variant's image when it is not the designation itself; it is an asset filename only and never an official designation.",
